+/// Tracks, within a function substitution, whether a reserved word could start next. As in
+/// Bash, the closing `}` is one in such a position: at the start of a command, after a
+/// group's `{ ...; }`. A `}` inside a word or among a command's arguments is text.
+#[derive(Debug)]
